1
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:06,340
Keeping Naoya
where I can always see him.

2
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:09,760
Hiding him away.

3
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:14,320
I want him all to myself.

4
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,020
Having him live in my territory.

5
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:28,230
He's taking too long.

6
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:34,010
(I'm going to the supermarket first, then
I'll head over.) It's been over two hours.

7
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,260
Calm down.

8
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:41,640
He probably just got held up by something.

9
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:48,020
While Naoya was sick,

10
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:50,560
whenever I went to his apartment,

11
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:54,070
he was always lying in bed.

12
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,210
Even though I wanted
him to get back on his feet,

13
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,240
a part of me also felt incredibly happy.

14
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,870
Even your feet are wet.

15
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:07,180
Lick them clean.

16
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:10,570
Understood.

17
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:23,220
You really do whatever you're told.

18
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:28,850
Could you even kiss me if I told you to?

19
00:01:46,390 --> 00:01:49,790
I once decided to have no other desires
but to wait for orders.

20
00:01:51,690 --> 00:01:53,150
But compared to back then,

21
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,460
my desires have grown much deeper.

22
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
"The Servant Prince" (Episode 7)

23
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,720
I refuse.

24
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,920
I have no intention of ever going back.

25
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:25,700
That's what I came here to tell you.

26
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:33,850
You're getting more and
more like your mother.

27
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,320
When my mother was alive,

28
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:45,030
she was never treated decently by you.

29
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,260
Shut up.

30
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,060
Please listen to me.

31
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,980
If you have a problem with how I do things,
then do it all yourself.

32
00:03:55,730 --> 00:03:57,790
Please don't yell.

33
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,060
Even so, rebelling against him

34
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:04,240
only seemed to make her situation worse.

35
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,500
Why were those two even married?

36
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:16,240
I heard it was a passionate
romance back then.

37
00:04:16,290 --> 00:04:18,589
They even defied the previous
generation's objections.

38
00:04:18,590 --> 00:04:19,590
Wow...

39
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:36,060
Naoya, you don't need to look
so worried. It's fine.

40
00:04:37,690 --> 00:04:41,600
Despite how he looks,
he actually has a cute side.

41
00:04:45,570 --> 00:04:46,630
But...

42
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:51,760
It's my father's fault
that my mother died so young.

43
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,760
Tatsuki.

44
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:11,680
Are you here again?

45
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,809
I even set up a chance
for you to meet your father.

46
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:17,200
You really are something else.

47
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:21,710
Anyway, let me meet
that guy with the glasses this time.

48
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:22,880
Huh?

49
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,250
You've got to be kidding.

50
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,700
Why would I do that?

51
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:28,200
Wait.

52
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,840
I thought I told you
to watch your attitude.

53
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:38,000
What are you doing?

54
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:39,330
Crap.

55
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,010
Takaaki, stop!

56
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:49,360
If you want to crush him,
use something other than violence.

57
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,720
Got it.

58
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,080
Let's go.

59
00:06:07,990 --> 00:06:09,760
What is wrong with you guys?

60
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:15,090
Looks like your plan to act as a broker
for a new contract is ruined.

61
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,620
Don't come back.

62
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:38,520
Let's move.

63
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:40,730
Huh?

64
00:06:40,731 --> 00:06:41,769
If possible, rather than
a luxury apartment,

65
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:43,850
I'd prefer a small house
where we can live together.

66
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:50,320
Are you against it?

67
00:06:57,730 --> 00:06:58,830
I want to live with you.

68
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,570
Great answer.

69
00:07:22,370 --> 00:07:23,960
Should we whip up something to eat?

70
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:27,130
I got a recipe for some delicious pancakes.

71
00:07:57,530 --> 00:08:00,050
Alright, all done.

72
00:08:00,350 --> 00:08:01,769
Oh, that looks so good.

73
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:02,770
Right?

74
00:08:02,910 --> 00:08:04,130
Okay, let's plate it.

75
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:04,900
Got it.

76
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:05,940
Takaaki, over here.

77
00:08:07,370 --> 00:08:08,980
Okay, thanks.

78
00:08:13,190 --> 00:08:14,550
It looks delicious.

79
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:20,550
Let's eat.

80
00:08:32,350 --> 00:08:33,550
So fluffy and chewy.

81
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:36,650
And it's even gluten-free.

82
00:08:38,590 --> 00:08:39,700
Let me try some too.

83
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:47,970
Mmm...

84
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:49,630
Yeah.

85
00:08:50,650 --> 00:08:51,690
You made it perfectly.

86
00:08:52,570 --> 00:08:53,570
Come to think of it,

87
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:56,346
this is the first time I've cooked for you
since I made mapo tofu, right?

88
00:08:56,370 --> 00:08:57,370
Yeah.

89
00:08:57,990 --> 00:09:01,370
Up until now,
I've always had you cook for me.

90
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:04,960
Thank you so much for everything.

91
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:17,850
I cook for you
because I want to.

92
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:25,290
Having Naoya eat my food

93
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:33,670
is an incredibly happy time for me.

94
00:09:39,930 --> 00:09:44,150
If I really get to live with Naoya,

95
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,950
every day will just
keep going like this.

96
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:57,210
At the end of the day,

97
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:04,530
the moment I close my eyes,
Naoya will always be right beside me.

98
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,560
I ended up not sleeping at all.

99
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:35,270
Good morning.

100
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:36,730
Good morning.

101
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:37,780
You're up early.

102
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:41,570
Yeah, I wanted to organize some files.

103
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:45,530
And breakfast too.

104
00:11:46,390 --> 00:11:48,350
Since we had leftover
ingredients from yesterday.

105
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,750
I'd expect nothing less from you.

106
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:55,790
Alright.

107
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:57,050
Let's eat.

108
00:12:02,290 --> 00:12:03,590
Mmm, it's good.

109
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:21,830
Hey.

110
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:28,840
Once we start living together, I'll
cook a lot of different dishes for you too.

111
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:38,670
What's wrong?

112
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,550
Oh, nothing.

113
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:48,640
Mmm, it's delicious.

114
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:27,600
(Property Information)

115
00:13:39,910 --> 00:13:40,910
Hello?

116
00:13:42,190 --> 00:13:43,190
Thank you.

117
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,520
I just saw the email.

118
00:13:46,410 --> 00:13:48,130
Please let me view the property right away.

119
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:51,540
Yeah.

120
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,180
That's right.

121
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:16,270
You really managed to
find such a great place.

122
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,310
Yeah.

123
00:14:17,470 --> 00:14:20,370
A place that met our criteria
just opened up. It was a huge help.

124
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:29,090
We'll be living here starting today.

125
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:33,340
Just the two of us.

126
00:14:34,570 --> 00:14:35,570
Yeah.

127
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:37,150
We will.

128
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,300
That's enough talk.

129
00:14:46,730 --> 00:14:47,730
Leave.

130
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:49,150
No way.

131
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:52,140
Please give me one more,
just one more chance.

132
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:53,449
I'll definitely meet your
expectations next time.

133
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:54,350
Take him away.

134
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:55,599
Understood.

135
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:56,560
Please leave.

136
00:14:56,561 --> 00:14:58,229
Please wait, President Goto.

137
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,310
At least take a look at this.

138
00:15:00,450 --> 00:15:03,190
I have exclusive
information about your son.

139
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:07,400
It won't hurt you to listen.

140
00:15:08,090 --> 00:15:09,090
What?

141
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:15,490
The other day,

142
00:15:15,810 --> 00:15:20,390
when I visited Sato Takaaki's apartment,
I happened to witness this scene.

143
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:27,650
Those two...

144
00:15:29,070 --> 00:15:30,270
So they are involved?

145
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:35,589
No wonder that man
messed with our company's system...

146
00:15:35,590 --> 00:15:36,590
What do you think?

147
00:15:37,030 --> 00:15:38,869
Do you need me to
investigate further for you?

148
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:39,870
No.

149
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:41,230
That won't be necessary.
Huh?

150
00:15:43,130 --> 00:15:43,940
Show him out.

151
00:15:43,941 --> 00:15:45,169
You can't be serious, President.

152
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:47,230
President,
I still have more to say!

153
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:51,490
Let go of me!
President! President!

154
00:16:13,310 --> 00:16:15,109
Oh, you want to make pasta?

155
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:16,110
Yes.

156
00:16:16,190 --> 00:16:18,470
I want to add more signature
dishes to my repertoire.

157
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:20,520
Yeah, of course.

158
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:22,590
Wait.

159
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:26,580
Are you planning to work in the
kitchen too, not just the front of house?

160
00:16:27,410 --> 00:16:28,410
No way.

161
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:29,820
That would be too much for me.

162
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:32,030
It's just...

163
00:16:33,590 --> 00:16:34,590
Just?

164
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:39,510
I've never cooked for anyone before.

165
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:44,180
So I want to learn how to make
it properly with my own hands.

166
00:16:45,730 --> 00:16:47,340
That's a great mindset.

167
00:16:49,330 --> 00:16:51,549
Alright, besides pasta,

168
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:54,550
I'll teach you a few
practical home recipes too.

169
00:16:55,470 --> 00:16:56,630
Thank you.

170
00:16:56,670 --> 00:16:57,790
I appreciate it.

171
00:17:04,410 --> 00:17:05,410
I'm home.

172
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:07,810
Oh, welcome back.

173
00:17:08,150 --> 00:17:09,370
Perfect timing.

174
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,480
Wow.

175
00:17:11,430 --> 00:17:12,690
You made this?

176
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,200
Yep.

177
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:18,080
Come on, sit down while it's hot.

178
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:21,830
- Okay.
- Enjoy.

179
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,800
It's delicious.

180
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:37,860
It tastes like it's from a restaurant.

181
00:17:38,350 --> 00:17:39,350
Right?

182
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:42,770
I might have a talent
for this, surprisingly.

183
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,250
Mmm, so good.

184
00:17:56,710 --> 00:17:57,710
Ah.

185
00:17:58,030 --> 00:18:00,590
Are the numbers here a bit off?

186
00:18:01,130 --> 00:18:02,669
Huh? Where?

187
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:03,670
Right here.

188
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:06,500
Oh, you're right.

189
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:09,460
Thanks a lot.
Yeah.

190
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,280
Your toothpaste tastes really minty.

191
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:27,740
I bought it on a business trip overseas.
I really like it.

192
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:30,020
Is the mint too strong?

193
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,000
No.

194
00:18:31,170 --> 00:18:32,570
It's cool and refreshing.

195
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:49,850
See? It's pretty nice, right?

196
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:03,930
To think I get to spend
every day like this with Naoya.

197
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:08,810
Can my heart really take this?

198
00:19:17,930 --> 00:19:19,510
Ah, is that Furuya?

199
00:19:19,550 --> 00:19:20,550
What's wrong?

200
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:23,870
Huh?

201
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:26,850
Yeah, I got it.

202
00:19:27,490 --> 00:19:28,490
I'll be right there.

203
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:32,210
What's wrong?

204
00:19:32,930 --> 00:19:34,880
It's nothing. Just a minor issue.

205
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:37,710
Sorry, I'm heading out.

206
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:40,800
Okay, take care.

207
00:19:42,650 --> 00:19:43,750
No, no, no.

208
00:19:44,150 --> 00:19:45,260
This is so sudden.

209
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:47,130
Yeah, it's ridiculous.

210
00:19:50,150 --> 00:19:52,210
Good morning.

211
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,330
Hey, did something happen?

212
00:19:55,870 --> 00:20:00,070
Goto-kun, HQ actually sent a notice.

213
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:03,910
They're not renewing the lease
for this store.

214
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:06,906
(Store Closure Notice) They said we
have to close by the end of next month.

215
00:20:06,930 --> 00:20:08,160
Wait, why?

216
00:20:08,590 --> 00:20:10,210
It's not like our sales are bad.

217
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:12,710
Did they raise the rent or something?

218
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,770
Anyway, I'll go to HQ and find out.

219
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:16,920
I'm counting on you.

220
00:20:17,690 --> 00:20:18,690
Goto-kun.

221
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:19,929
I'll leave the store to you.

222
00:20:19,930 --> 00:20:20,930
Got it.

223
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:27,680
Why go this far?

224
00:20:27,990 --> 00:20:30,029
Why are you so obsessed with my brother?

225
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:31,349
That's none of your business.

226
00:20:31,350 --> 00:20:32,550
Of course it is.

227
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,520
I'm an employee of this company too.

228
00:20:35,230 --> 00:20:38,070
And I'm also your son.

229
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,240
I'm in a hurry.

230
00:20:43,290 --> 00:20:44,550
Is that all you have to say?

231
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:05,610
Thank you. Please come again.

232
00:21:14,270 --> 00:21:16,910
Why close the store so suddenly?

233
00:21:19,770 --> 00:21:20,770
Could it be...

234
00:21:24,810 --> 00:21:25,690
Huh...

235
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:27,526
Something happened
to Takaaki's company too?

236
00:21:27,550 --> 00:21:31,300
A major partnership fell through.

237
00:21:32,390 --> 00:21:34,390
They just brushed us
off with a canned email.

238
00:21:35,130 --> 00:21:37,210
How could that be? Are you okay?

239
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,710
I'm fine.

240
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:41,840
There are plenty of companies
that want to switch to our system.

241
00:21:42,710 --> 00:21:46,300
Besides, I wouldn't build a company

242
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:48,150
that would crumble
over something like this.

243
00:21:48,970 --> 00:21:49,970
Huh?

244
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:51,810
More importantly,

245
00:21:52,870 --> 00:21:55,080
I've connected the dots.

246
00:21:57,030 --> 00:22:02,040
The boss of the client who canceled on us
is your father's college classmate.

247
00:22:02,910 --> 00:22:06,250
And I heard they're still very close.

248
00:22:08,050 --> 00:22:11,390
The developer of the building our
store is in is also Goto Construction.

249
00:22:13,070 --> 00:22:14,070
Takaaki.

250
00:22:14,290 --> 00:22:15,290
I'm so sorry.

251
00:22:15,970 --> 00:22:18,290
My dad is definitely the
one pulling the strings.

252
00:22:19,910 --> 00:22:21,790
Because of him, even
you got dragged into this.

253
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:27,940
And when I think about
my coworkers...

254
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:30,550
Hey, Takaaki.

255
00:22:31,970 --> 00:22:34,660
Actually, a while ago,
Tachiki arranged for me to meet my dad.

256
00:22:35,310 --> 00:22:36,310
Huh?

257
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:41,080
My dad said he'd forgive me if I
got on my knees and apologized.

258
00:22:42,470 --> 00:22:44,320
So I told him clearly.

259
00:22:50,710 --> 00:22:52,240
I won't hold back anymore.

260
00:22:55,970 --> 00:22:56,970
Takaaki.

261
00:22:58,040 --> 00:22:59,670
This is an order from me.

262
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:05,520
Deal a fatal blow to my dad's company.

263
00:23:08,650 --> 00:23:09,650
Understood.

264
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:12,400
As long as I don't use violence,

265
00:23:13,010 --> 00:23:15,720
I can use any means necessary
to crush it completely, right?

266
00:23:15,770 --> 00:23:16,770
Of course.

267
00:23:19,110 --> 00:23:20,350
No need to hold back.

268
00:23:23,570 --> 00:23:24,570
You can do it, right?

269
00:23:26,370 --> 00:23:27,370
Yeah.

270
00:24:30,100 --> 00:24:31,200
(Next Episode Preview)

271
00:24:31,290 --> 00:24:33,780
If we attack there,
we can deal him a fatal blow.

272
00:24:33,830 --> 00:24:34,969
Just go all out.

273
00:24:34,970 --> 00:24:36,050
Got it.

274
00:24:36,630 --> 00:24:38,030
Brother, please come back.

275
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:39,520
Go gather some allies, Yuma.

276
00:24:39,570 --> 00:24:41,540
To fight against that old man,

277
00:24:41,570 --> 00:24:42,966
I'm going to live my life with this guy.

278
00:24:42,990 --> 00:24:44,290
Right, Takaaki?
